R1 viability.closure_functor
  Lean target:
    ERIEC.ViabilityClosure.viabilityClosureFunctor_left_natural
  Type boundary:
    f is a ViableSystemIso, hence f.mapConfig is an Equiv. The theorem is
    quantified over every K.
  Prior defect:
    Set(keys)==source and Set(values)==target accepted a collision when the
    source had greater cardinality than the target.
  Repair:
    the additive all-K checker now validates duplicate-free carriers, mapping
    totality, image membership, injectivity, surjectivity, cardinality equality,
    and both inverse round trips before evaluating naturality.
  Required counterexample:
    [:a,:b,:c] -> [:x,:y] with a->x, b->x, c->y is rejected as non-bijective.

R2 bridge.hinge_strict_functor
  Lean target:
    ERIEC.BridgeFunctor.strictHingeClassifier_identity_intertwines
  Type boundary:
    StrictHingeData preorder is X.data.holds iff Y.data.holds. This is distinct
    from CompleteHingeData's one-way HingeForward implication.
  Prior defect:
    the additive checker trusted an externally supplied arrow_valid Bool.
  Repair:
    a finite-data additive method recomputes both holds predicates with Act,
    derives arrow_valid as source_holds == target_holds, validates both
    independently supplied loop candidates, and then decides intertwining.
    The legacy Bool method remains only for compatibility and is not the exact
    contract evidence path.
  Required counterexample:
    source holds, target does not, and a mutated target loop is rejected without
    any caller-supplied arrow premise.

R3 reference_models.v5_1
  Lean target:
    ERIEC.RefModel.reference_models
  Type boundary:
    the closed theorem is exactly the three literal RefState next equations.
  Prior defect:
    v5.1 acceptance was gated by fields belonging only to three later witness
    contracts, producing a false negative for a states/next-only candidate.
  Repair:
    a dedicated exact two-field path validates the duplicate-free complete
    carrier and literal next table. The existing exact full candidate shape is
    still accepted for the combined four-contract API. Partial shapes and
    unknown extra fields are rejected.
  Evidence cases:
    the minimal states/next candidate passes; mutated next, missing state,
    unknown state, and unexpected-field candidates fail.

